#!/bin/sh

# temprary fix for the eDP-1 not getting a clean modeset on first boot.
# no much time to find the best way to fix it ... i ll do it later or i wont i dont really know XD

# this is LLM generated i didnt read it or anything ... it working for now so ...
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Force a fresh modeset on the laptop panel (eDP-1) a couple seconds into login.
#
# On a cold first boot the AMD-driven primary output sometimes never gets a
# clean modeset under the NVIDIA(card0)+AMD(card1) multi-GPU setup and stays
# black, while the NVIDIA-driven HDMI output comes up fine. A full re-login
# fixes it by redoing the modeset; this replicates that by toggling DPMS on
# eDP-1, which forces a fresh modeset and lights up the panel.
#
# Why DPMS and not a mode-switch: switching eDP-1 to a throwaway resolution and
# back also forces a modeset, but it leaves the panel powered on the whole time
# and stamps a frozen software-cursor "ghost" onto the screen that never gets
# repainted. DPMS physically blanks the panel, so nothing can linger.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT disable/re-enable the output to force the modeset.
# Disabling removes the wl_output, which crashes xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
# (CSharedPointer<CCWlOutput>::_delete) and breaks screen sharing. DPMS keeps
# the output present, so the portal survives.

sleep 2
# Power the panel off and back on. This forces the same fresh modeset that a
# re-login does, lighting up eDP-1 — but unlike a mode-switch it physically
# blanks the panel, so it cannot leave a stale software-cursor "ghost" stamped
# on screen. DPMS keeps the wl_output present, so it does NOT crash
# xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland the way disabling the output would.
#
# This config uses Hyprland's Lua parser, where `hyprctl dispatch` is dead —
# dispatchers must be run as hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.<name>(...)) via `hyprctl eval`.
hyprctl eval 'hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.dpms({ action = "disable" }))'
sleep 1
hyprctl eval 'hl.dispatch(hl.dsp.dpms({ action = "enable" }))'
